    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2UyR1EqUZEYkn7v6jWwzw5D)_\n\nFollows #330.\n\n## The load error\n`Cannot open load file ... sp-collection-query-tables-book` is not a code bug: `sp-collection-query-tables-book.el` (and the `-book-widget` file) are in `main`, but `~/.config/emacs-modular` is a tree of Stow links, and a file added by a pull has no link until you re-stow. Fix on your side, once after pulling:\n\n```\ncd ~/dotfiles && stow -R emacs-modular\n```\n(this is in `stow-migration/README.org`). No code change is needed for it; the doc now says so.\n\n## What this PR changes: where saved views live\n- `sp-collec-query-views-file` now defaults to `views/sp-collection-query-tables-views.el` **inside the configuration**, and that file is tracked in the repo (empty at first). After `stow -R emacs-modular` it is a link into `~/dotfiles`, so a view saved from the menu (`S`) or with `sp-collec-query-view-save-from-dblock` shows up in `git status` there, ready to commit. Nothing has to be copied or moved by hand.\n- The older locations (below `sp-etc-dir`, and directly in the config) are still read until the new file holds a view; the next save writes the new file, carrying those views over.\n- Built-in views stay in the code (`sp-collec-query-views-defaults`).\n\n## Tested\n- 6 template tests (new: empty tracked file falls back to the older file, and a save carries its views over) and 7 book tests pass in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- **Not run:** writing through the Stow link on your Mac (it relies on `write-region` following the link), or the interactive commands.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edit, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBucimHCJ8fQCvMaMF)_",
